Check client transactions with remote writes pushed over cdb2api: remote-only
and mixed local/remote transactions commit and rollback correctly, a local
update or delete after a pushed remote write runs in a proper local
transaction, a remote-only transaction is rolled back when the client
disconnects, and the transaction effects are reported correctly.

The same transactions run from stored procedures: outside a client
transaction (the implicit transaction of the procedure, db:begin/db:commit
and db:rollback, a procedure failing after its writes), and inside a client
transaction.
